# EJE Job Card Management System — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never
# be committed. NOTHING in this file is a real credential.
#
# The browser demonstration needs none of these: it runs entirely client-side
# and `npm test`, `npm run build` and the browser suites all pass with no
# database present. These are for the PostgreSQL work.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The connection string Drizzle uses for migrations and for the repositories.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://eje:change-me@localhost:5432/eje_dev

# A SEPARATE database for integration tests. The test suite truncates it
# between cases, so it must never point at development or production data —
# `db:test` refuses to run against a URL whose database name is not clearly a
# test database.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgres://eje:change-me@localhost:5432/eje_test

# Logs every SQL statement. Development only; noisy.
# DRIZZLE_DEBUG=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which persistence the server uses
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Decided in `src/data/backend.ts`, from this environment and from nothing a
# browser can set. Leave it unset: the presence of DATABASE_URL is what means a
# database exists, which is the honest signal.
#
#   demo      — force the demonstration store, even where a database is
#               configured. What a sales laptop wants.
#   postgres  — demand PostgreSQL, so a missing DATABASE_URL fails loudly
#               instead of quietly serving demonstration data to the business.
#
# EJE_PERSISTENCE=postgres
